<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martynas Mažvydas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–<a href="/years/1563">1563</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martynas Mažvydas was a Lutheran pastor and the author of the first printed book in the Lithuanian language, a catechism published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a> in 1547. Educated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-konigsberg">University of Königsberg</a>, he served as a pastor in Ragainė in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Ducal Prussia</a>. His catechism, which includes a short primer and hymns, marks the beginning of Lithuanian written literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martynas-mazvydas.jpg" alt="Martynas Mažvydas" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martynas Mažvydas, who lived in 1510 (or 1520) – 1563. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CATECHISMVSA_PRAsty_Szadei_(in_Lithuanian_language)_by_Martynas_Ma%C5%BEvydas,_published_in_K%C3%B6nigsberg,_1547_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
